Long-duration UAV missions are limited by battery capacity, which forces agents to leave the formation and jeopardizes mission continuity. We propose a fully decentralized, communication-centric multi-agent system that enables persistent formation flight by allowing UAVs to autonomously replace depleted members and to hand over leadership without any central controller. The approach is implemented in ROS using the ALICA coordination framework and evaluated in Gazebo simulations that demonstrate resilient formation maintenance and seamless leader/follower handovers.